    r1p3:"This website is that output. Built on the member company database, it implements a four-stage matching process running from qualification through to curated pre-matching.",


    r3t:"AI-based battery data analytics and lifetime prediction",
    r3w:"Kongju National University / HUBA · BME",
    r3p1:"Laboratory testing is accurate but slow and expensive, and cannot be applied to every battery in the field. This area of work studies how to estimate battery condition from the voltage, current, and temperature data that a battery management system already collects during normal operation.",
    r3p2:"A lithium-ion cell degrades through several coupled mechanisms. Growth of the solid-electrolyte interphase consumes cyclable lithium and raises internal resistance; loss of active material reduces capacity; and under cold or fast-charging conditions lithium plating accelerates both capacity fade and safety risk. The externally observable signals reflect the combined effect of these hidden processes, which makes state estimation an inverse problem \u2014 and a natural target for data-driven methods.",
    r3h1:"State of health estimation",
    r3c1:"Family", r3c2:"Principle", r3c3:"Limitation",
    r3m1:"Direct measurement", r3m1p:"Coulomb counting, full charge/discharge, internal resistance measurement", r3m1l:"Time-consuming and impractical in the field",
    r3m2:"Model-based", r3m2p:"Parameter identification on equivalent-circuit or electrochemical models", r3m2l:"Sensitive to parameter drift and operating conditions",
    r3m3:"Data-driven", r3m3p:"Machine learning learns the relationship between signals and condition", r3m3l:"Requires data and labels; generalisation is the challenge",
    r3p3:"Where data is scarce and interpretability matters, classical methods such as Gaussian process regression and support-vector regression remain attractive; where sufficient field data exists, deep architectures \u2014 convolutional, recurrent, and transformer \u2014 perform better. The practical conclusion is that method selection should follow data availability.",
    r3h2:"Remaining useful life prediction",
    r3p4:"Remaining useful life is the time or number of cycles left before an end-of-life threshold, conventionally 80% of nominal capacity for first-life automotive use. Two issues matter in practice.",
    r3l1:"<b>Early prediction</b> \u2014 forecasting end-of-life from only the first cycles allows screening and binning decisions to be made early, but is difficult because early-life signals correlate weakly with eventual failure",
    r3l2:"<b>Uncertainty quantification</b> \u2014 a point estimate without confidence bounds is of limited use for maintenance or reuse decisions, so methods reporting calibrated uncertainty are preferred",
    r3l3:"<b>Capacity regeneration</b> \u2014 capacity partially recovers after rest, producing non-monotonic degradation curves that purely trend-based predictors handle poorly, which has motivated decomposition-based and hybrid models",
    r3h3:"Fault detection and anomaly analysis",
    r3p5:"Undetected internal short circuits, thermal abuse, connection faults, or progressive cell inconsistency can lead to thermal runaway. Unsupervised anomaly detection operating on commonly available signals such as cell voltage, without labels, is used to provide early warning.",
    r3h4:"Methodological taxonomy",
    r3d1:"Approach", r3d2:"Core idea", r3d3:"Trade-off",
    r3x1:"Residual-driven", r3x1p:"Reconstruct signals; residual error flags anomalies", r3x1l:"Easy to deploy; low interpretability",
    r3x2:"Feature-driven", r3x2p:"Extract health indicators, then model", r3x2l:"Interpretable; depends on feature design",
    r3x3:"Distribution-driven", r3x3p:"Cluster and distribution analysis separates normal from abnormal", r3x3l:"Label-free; sensitive to assumptions",
    r3x4:"Physics-driven", r3x4p:"Integrate physical or domain models with learning", r3x4l:"Data-efficient; model-dependent",
    r3h5:"Transfer learning and domain adaptation",
    r3p6:"Laboratory data is clean but scarce; field data is abundant but noisy. Transfer learning carries knowledge from a data-rich domain to a data-scarce one to bridge that gap. Evaluating candidate methods on public datasets first means that when local data becomes available, only the adaptation step remains rather than the entire modelling effort.",

    r4t:"Environmental impact assessment and circular economy",
    r4w:"Ewha Womans University / HUBA · ELTE · HUN-REN",
    r4p1:"This work measures and reduces the pollutants arising from battery manufacturing and recycling. The Environmental, Public Health and Safety Unit comprises two research sub-units and one support group.",
    r4h1:"Monitoring and assessment sub-unit",
    r4l1:"<b>Monitoring and analytics group</b> \u2014 identifies and prioritises the pollutants most critical to the battery industry, including NMP, hydrogen fluoride, heavy metals, and PFAS. Carries out field monitoring, laboratory-grade chemical analysis, and time- and location-based pollution modelling",
    r4l2:"<b>LCA and risk assessment group</b> \u2014 quantifies environmental impact through lifecycle assessment, and assesses chemical and human health risk through toxicological modelling and exposure scenario analysis",
    r4h2:"Sustainable technology development sub-unit",
    r4l3:"<b>Pollutant control group</b> \u2014 develops VOC abatement, hydrogen fluoride scrubbing, and high-salinity wastewater treatment technologies",
    r4l4:"<b>Recycling technology group</b> \u2014 researches low-chemical hydrometallurgy, direct cathode recycling, and material recovery strategies for next-generation batteries",
    r4call:"<b>A joint project with the Research Centre for Natural Sciences in Hungary is in preparation.</b> It concerns a hybrid recycling platform combining eco-friendly electrochemical leaching with carbon material recovery. Redox-assisted dissolution and green solvents would selectively extract lithium, cobalt, and nickel from black mass while minimising secondary pollution, with graphite recovered in parallel from spent anodes to close the loop on electrode materials.",
    r4h3:"Regulatory and communication support group",
    r4p2:"Interprets the EU Battery Regulation, REACH, and permitting requirements to support compliance. Prepares LCA reports and carbon footprint disclosures, provides the data required for the battery passport, and manages coordination with government agencies, local communities, and partner organisations.",

    r5t:"The Yonsei pilot experiment",
    r5w:"Yonsei University",
    r5p1:"The full-scale laboratories will be built up over several years. Ahead of that, a small facility at Yonsei is running a pilot during the fourth year to test whether the methodology works in practice.",
    r5h1:"Experimental setup",
    r5p2:"Commercial lithium-ion cells representative of those in current electric vehicles are cycled across a range of temperatures, charge and discharge rates, and depths of discharge. Voltage, current, and temperature are collected at the resolution needed to train and validate AI models. The cell-level setup is sufficient to validate the core methodology, leaving module- and pack-level work to the full-scale laboratory.",
    r5h2:"Preliminary results",
    r5p3:"Under the conditions tested so far, the AI estimates track the laboratory-measured reference values closely. Validation continues through the fourth year, with the full set of results to be reported in the final deliverable.",
    r5h3:"Handover to full-scale operations",
    r5p4:"The pilot produces three things: a dataset that will serve as a reference point for later work, a documented methodology transferable to the Battery Passport and Data Analysis Unit and the Competency Test Unit, and evidence that KHBCC is doing technical work alongside institutional work. The last of these supports the case for follow-on funding.",

    lgT1:"Kongju Nat. Univ. · HUBA · BME", lgT2:"Kongju Nat. Univ. · HUBA · BME", lgT3:"Ewha Womans Univ. · HUBA · ELTE · HUN-REN",
